# A permission to cast a card leaves its alternative costs open (CR 601.2b, 118.9), whoever owns the card: Null Summoner's
# threshold ability lets Bot1 cast the Solitude it exiled from Bot2's hand, so Bot1 may evoke it (CR 702.74a) by exiling a white
# card from its own hand, Swords to Plowshares, with every mana source tapped. Solitude enters, exiles no creature (its target is
# "up to one"), and the evoke trigger sacrifices it: it goes to its owner's graveyard, Bot2's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
